---
/**
 * How it works, end to end: the developer's path to a cluster, the cluster
 * with an instance per organization and mero-kms, and the people and agents
 * who verify a node before they talk to their instance. Governance decisions
 * (releases, upgrades, outbound hosts) are marked where they gate the path.
 */
---

<figure class="cal-e2e not-content">
	<div class="lanes">
		<section class="lane">
			<span class="k">01 · Developer</span>
			<ol class="steps">
				<li><b>Write</b><span>Rust logic on the SDK, and a frontend</span></li>
				<li><b>Bundle &amp; sign</b><code>cargo mero bundle --key</code></li>
				<li><b>Publish</b><span>to the app registry, private to your org or public</span></li>
				<li><b>Deploy</b><span>from the Cloud console: shared or dedicated cluster</span></li>
			</ol>
		</section>

		<div class="flow" aria-hidden="true"><span>signed .mpk</span></div>

		<section class="lane cluster">
			<span class="k">02 · Cluster · attested Intel TDX nodes</span>
			<div class="nodes" aria-hidden="true">
				<span>node</span><span>node</span><span>node</span>
			</div>
			<p class="note">Every node checks the package signature before it runs it.</p>
			<div class="orgs">
				<div class="org">
					<span class="o">Org · acme</span>
					<b>notes</b>
					<span class="i">own state · init {'{'}"title": "Acme"{'}'}</span>
				</div>
				<div class="org">
					<span class="o">Org · globex</span>
					<b>notes</b>
					<span class="i">own state · init {'{'}"title": "Globex"{'}'}</span>
				</div>
			</div>
			<p class="note">Each instance is replicated by its own Raft log across three nodes.</p>
			<div class="kms">
				<b>mero-kms</b>
				<span>releases a node's storage key only after its quote matches the signed release</span>
			</div>
			<div class="gov">
				<span class="k">Governance · fixed at genesis, attested</span>
				<ul>
					<li><b>Node images</b> approved by the app's owner or the operator</li>
					<li><b>App upgrades</b> approved by the app's owner or the operator</li>
					<li><b>Outbound hosts</b> the manifest declares, approved before any call leaves</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<div class="flow back" aria-hidden="true"><span>verify, then seal</span></div>

		<section class="lane">
			<span class="k">03 · People &amp; agents</span>
			<ol class="steps">
				<li><b>Verify</b><span>the node's quote against the signed release</span></li>
				<li><b>Seal</b><span>open an encrypted channel to the key the quote binds</span></li>
				<li><b>Sign in</b><span>a passkey for people, a scoped API key for agents</span></li>
				<li><b>Call</b><span>their org's instance; every answer carries a receipt</span></li>
			</ol>
			<p class="note">mero-js · Python · Rust · meroctl · the Calimero MCP</p>
		</section>
	</div>
	<figcaption>
		One signed bundle, any number of organizations. Nobody operating the nodes, Calimero included, can read an instance's
		data, and every client can check that before it sends anything.
	</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.cal-e2e {
		margin: 1.75rem 0;
	}
	.lanes {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1.35fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: 10px;
		align-items: stretch;
	}
	.lane {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 10px;
		padding: 14px;
		border: 1px solid var(--cal-rule);
		background: var(--cal-card);
		min-width: 0;
	}
	.lane.cluster {
		border-color: var(--cal-ink);
		background: var(--cal-paper-2);
		box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--cal-hard);
	}
	.k {
		font: 600 0.7rem/1.4 var(--sl-font-mono);
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--cal-seal);
	}
	.steps {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		display: grid;
		gap: 8px;
		counter-reset: s;
	}
	.steps li {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1px;
		padding-left: 26px;
		position: relative;
		counter-increment: s;
	}
	.steps li::before {
		content: counter(s);
		position: absolute;
		left: 0;
		top: 0;
		width: 18px;
		height: 18px;
		display: grid;
		place-items: center;
		border: 1px solid var(--cal-ink);
		font: 600 0.68rem/1 var(--sl-font-mono);
		color: var(--cal-ink);
	}
	.steps b {
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		color: var(--cal-ink);
	}
	.steps span,
	.steps code {
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		line-height: 1.4;
		color: var(--cal-ink-2);
	}
	.steps code {
		font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
		background: none;
		border: 0;
		padding: 0;
	}
	.nodes {
		display: flex;
		gap: 6px;
	}
	.nodes span {
		flex: 1;
		padding: 5px 0;
		text-align: center;
		border: 1px solid var(--cal-box-line);
		font: 500 0.7rem/1 var(--sl-font-mono);
		color: var(--cal-muted);
	}
	.orgs {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(130px, 1fr));
		gap: 8px;
	}
	.org {
		display: grid;
		gap: 2px;
		padding: 8px 10px;
		border: 1px solid var(--cal-seal);
		background: var(--cal-card);
	}
	.o {
		font: 600 0.66rem/1.3 var(--sl-font-mono);
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--cal-seal);
	}
	.org b {
		color: var(--cal-ink);
	}
	.i {
		font: 400 0.72rem/1.35 var(--sl-font-mono);
		color: var(--cal-muted);
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
	}
	.kms {
		display: grid;
		gap: 2px;
		padding: 8px 10px;
		border: 1px dashed var(--cal-box-line);
	}
	.kms b {
		font: 600 0.78rem/1.3 var(--sl-font-mono);
		color: var(--cal-ink);
	}
	.kms span {
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		color: var(--cal-ink-2);
	}
	.gov {
		display: grid;
		gap: 6px;
		padding-top: 10px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--cal-rule);
	}
	.gov ul {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		display: grid;
		gap: 4px;
	}
	.gov li {
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		line-height: 1.4;
		color: var(--cal-ink-2);
	}
	.gov b {
		color: var(--cal-ink);
	}
	.note {
		margin: 0;
		font: 400 0.74rem/1.45 var(--sl-font-mono);
		color: var(--cal-muted);
	}
	.flow {
		display: grid;
		place-items: center;
		position: relative;
		min-width: 22px;
	}
	.flow::before {
		content: '→';
		font: 600 1.3rem/1 var(--sl-font-mono);
		color: var(--cal-seal);
	}
	.flow.back::before {
		content: '⇄';
	}
	.flow span {
		position: absolute;
		top: calc(50% + 16px);
		writing-mode: vertical-rl;
		font: 500 0.64rem/1 var(--sl-font-mono);
		color: var(--cal-muted);
		white-space: nowrap;
	}
	figcaption {
		margin-top: 10px;
		font: 400 0.8rem/1.5 var(--sl-font-mono);
		color: var(--cal-muted);
	}
	@media (max-width: 56rem) {
		.lanes {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
		.flow {
			min-height: 34px;
		}
		.flow::before {
			transform: rotate(90deg);
		}
		.flow span {
			position: static;
			writing-mode: horizontal-tb;
			margin-top: 4px;
		}
		.flow {
			grid-auto-flow: column;
			gap: 10px;
		}
	}
</style>
